+# #615 evidence — toast visible while the consent banner is up
+
+Re-run of the bug-hunt evidence style for the fix: the toast stack moved from
+`fixed bottom-4 right-4 z-50` (hidden behind the consent banner) to
+`fixed top-20 right-4 z-[2147483001]` (below the in-flow header, one z-step
+above the banner's `2147483000`). `consent.js` is untouched.
+
+## What was tested
+
+`toast-overlay-evidence.html` loads the **real built assets** —
+`/server/priv/static/tailwind.css` and `/server/priv/static/consent.js` —
+plus a toast container carrying the **exact classes** from
+`client/src/components/toast.gleam` and the real OQ-5 copy
+(`copy.refcheck_toast_exported`). A fresh browser profile (no consent choice
+→ banner up) fires the toast 800ms after load and auto-dismisses it at 5.8s,
+mirroring the app's toast lifecycle.
+
+Drive: `python3 -m http.server 8899` + agent-browser, fresh
+`--session` per scenario. Screenshots below + the DOM geometry evals.
+
+## Results
+
+### Desktop — 1280×800 (`evidence-desktop-toast-banner.png`)
+
+```json
+{"viewport":[1280,800],
+ "bannerVisible":true,        "bannerBox":{"top":572,"bottom":784,...},
+ "toastVisible":true,         "toastBox":{"top":80,"bottom":152,...},
+ "toastOverlapsBanner":false,
+ "toastOverlapsBannerButton":false,
+ "toastZ":"2147483001","bannerZ":"2147483000"}
+```
+
+Screenshot (vision-verified): toast card top-right below the navy header;
+banner bottom-centered with all three buttons; **no overlap; no button
+covered**.
+
+### Mobile — 375×667 (`evidence-mobile-toast-banner.png`)
+
+```json
+{"viewport":[375,667],
+ "bannerVisible":true,        "bannerBox":{"top":295,"bottom":651,...},
+ "toastVisible":true,         "toastBox":{"top":80,"bottom":152,...},
+ "toastOverlapsBanner":false,
+ "toastOverlapsBannerButton":false,
+ "toastZ":"2147483001","bannerZ":"2147483000"}
+```
+
+Banner renders taller on mobile (356px) — still **no overlap** with the
+toast.
+
+### Banner clickability
+
+Clicked `[data-testid="consent-accept-all"]` → banner removed, consent
+persisted (`localStorage.rt_consent = set`). The banner stays fully
+interactive while the toast is up.
+
+### Degenerate corner — 320×480 + expanded Customize panel (`evidence-corner-tiny-viewport.png`)
+
+```json
+{"toastY":{"top":80,"bottom":152},"buttons":{"consent-reject-all":{"top":9,"bottom":52},
+ "consent-customize":{"top":60,"bottom":103},"consent-accept-all":{"top":111,"bottom":154},
+ "consent-save":{"top":400,"bottom":443}}}
+```
+
+With the customize panel open the banner is **666px tall — taller than the 480px
+viewport** (its heading/body are clipped off-screen with or without any toast).
+The banner's primary buttons therefore stop being bottom-aligned: they sit
+clipped near the top of the viewport (y≈9–154) where the top-anchored toast
+(y 80–152) lands. The toast is still visible (`toastVisible:true`, z 2147483001)
+and transiently overlaps the "Reject all" / "Customize" / "Accept all" row for
+its 5s lifetime (the toast is dismissible via its ✕ and auto-dismisses).
+
+**Constraint conflict (called out deliberately):** "toasts visible during the
+consent window" and "never cover the banner's interactive area" are mutually
+unsatisfiable in this corner — the banner is taller than the screen, so every
+pixel is banner. This fix chooses **toast visible** (the issue's primary
+acceptance); the alternative (toast z-index below the banner) would make the
+confirmation invisible — the original bug — in this same corner. The frozen
+spec's "never the bottom-aligned buttons" guarantee holds in every case where
+the buttons actually ARE bottom-aligned (any viewport the banner fits).
+Flagged in the PR's Decisions & rationale.
+
