+---
+title: 'bug-hunt UX fallout: unambiguous stepper label + toast visibility during consent window'
+type: 'bugfix'
+created: '2026-08-14'
+status: 'done'
+review_loop_iteration: 0
+baseline_commit: 'ba605ba'
+context: []
+---
+
+<frozen-after-approval reason="human-owned intent — do not modify unless human renegotiates">
+
+## Intent
+
+**Problem:** Two bug-hunt UX fallouts on the landlord dashboard. (1) The `viewed` application status renders as "Viewed" on the stepper, status pill, and detail page — a landlord reads it as "application opened" when it actually means "the viewing with the applicant was carried out". The transition INTO `viewed` mints the queued reference calls (RC2.2 A5), so a misread either never starts checks or fires them prematurely. (2) The cookie-consent banner (`consent.js`, bottom-anchored, `z-index:2147483000`) renders above the toast stack (`fixed bottom-4 right-4 z-50`), so every toast — including the refcheck "Attempt log copied" confirmation — is DOM-present but visually hidden while the banner is up.
+
+**Approach:** (1) Relabel every user-facing rendering of the status to the single term **"Viewing held"** (stepper stop, stepper `label_for_slug_opt` feeding the backward-confirm modal and audit trail, shared status pill, detail-page uppercase pill) and add a native `title` hint on the viewed stepper stop explaining that marking it starts the reference checks. Internal slugs, DB enum, trigger logic, and `vacancy.viewed_at` stay `viewed`. (2) Move the toast stack from bottom-right to top-right, just below the in-flow header (`fixed top-20 right-4`), so it never geometrically overlaps the bottom-anchored banner, and raise its z-index one step above the banner's (`z-[2147483001]`) as belt-and-braces for the extreme corner case (tiny viewport + expanded customize panel). `consent.js` is untouched.
+
+## Boundaries & Constraints
+
+**Always:**
+- ONE user-facing term — "Viewing held" — on every surface the status renders (stepper stop, `label_for_slug_opt`, status pill, detail-page pill). Internal identifiers stay `viewed`: DB enum, API slugs, `data-testid` values, `stepper-stop-viewed` ids, logs, migration file.
+- The toast must be visible while the consent banner is up; the banner must remain visible AND clickable at all times — never cover its interactive (button) area, never dismiss or move it.
+- No em dashes in any new copy (no-em-dash ruling). Brand voice: calm, specific, outcome-oriented.
+- New user-facing copy strings go in `client/src/copy.gleam` where the component does not already inline its label (the pre-existing inline status-label pattern in the stepper/pill components is left as-is for the relabel, but the new hint copy is a `copy.gleam` const).
+- Full local suite green (`make test-all`) and `make format` before the PR; `make build-client` output re-checked after every client change.
+
+**Ask First:** none expected — the briefing delegates the label wording and the toast mechanism choice to this job; both choices are recorded in the PR's Decisions & rationale.
+
+**Never:**
+- No DB enum change (`20260808120000_add_viewed_application_status.sql` stays `viewed`); no refcheck trigger logic change; no `vacancy.viewed_at` touch (unrelated ad-view counter).
+- No `consent.js` logic changes: the banner is not moved, resized, dismissed, or re-layered below app modals.
+- No stepper-order changes, no broader copy sweep, no #611 input-path work (that's PR #616's).
+- No toast timing/auto-dismiss changes, no modal-layering changes, no Tailwind config changes.
+
+## I/O & Edge-Case Matrix
+
+| Scenario | Input / State | Expected Output / Behavior | Error Handling |
+|----------|--------------|---------------------------|----------------|
+| HAPPY_PATH | Application in `viewed` status; landlord on detail page | Stepper stop, detail pill, status pill, audit-trail label all read "Viewing held" (detail pill uppercase "VIEWING HELD") | N/A |
+| Stepper_hint | Landlord hovers the Viewed stop | Native tooltip: "Mark when you've carried out the viewing. Reference checks start here." | N/A |
+| Backward_modal | Landlord clicks a stop behind `viewed` (target slug "viewed") | Modal copy "Move {name} back to Viewing held?" | N/A |
+| Toast_during_consent | Fresh profile (no consent choice); any toast fires while banner is up | Toast visible (top-right); banner still visible + clickable; toast box does not intersect banner button area | If viewport is tiny and the customize panel makes the banner tall, toast may transiently overlap the banner's upper body-text region — never the bottom-aligned buttons; toast auto-dismisses in 5s |
+| Internal_slug | DB / API / logs / data-testids reference the status | Unchanged: `viewed` / `stepper-stop-viewed` / `status-pill-viewed` | N/A |
+
+</frozen-after-approval>
