+## Design Notes
+
+**Label choice — "Viewing held"** (briefing candidate, retained): reads unambiguously as "the viewing took place" (action-complete), stays calm and specific per brand voice, and is the least awkward of the candidates inside the generic modal template "Move {name} back to {status}?". Internal identifiers (`viewed`, `stepper-stop-viewed`, `status-pill-viewed`, `application.Viewed`) stay untouched so the DB enum, trigger hook (`trigger.gleam` keys off `app_sql.Viewed`), API slugs, and bug-hunt testids do not churn.
+
+**Toast mechanism — reposition + raise, not re-layer the banner:** the banner deliberately out-ranks everything (`z-index:2147483000`, above the z-50 modal system) because consent must stay visible until a choice is made — lowering it would put it under modal backdrops. Raising only the toast stack (`z-[2147483001]`) and moving it top-right (`top-20 right-4`, just below the in-flow `h-16` header) gives: (a) no geometric overlap with the bottom-anchored banner in any normal viewport — the banner's interactive buttons stay fully exposed; (b) z-index above the banner only as belt-and-braces for the extreme corner (tiny viewport + expanded customize panel) where a toast can transiently overlap the banner's upper body-text region but never its bottom-aligned buttons. DOM order already renders toasts last at z-50, so toasts already sit above the z-50 modals; raising the value does not change modal layering (no regression). `consent.js` is not touched.
